SUMMARY:Music of the Baroque: Vivaldi & Friends
DESCRIPTION:VIVALDI Concerto for Strings in G Minor\nSAMMARTINI Sinfonia in F Major\nGEMINIANI Concerto\, “La Follia”\nCORELLI Concerto Grosso\, op. 6\, no. 11\nNARDINI Concerto for Violin\, op. 1\, no. 1\nVIVALDI Concerto for 2 Violins in G Minor\nPUGNANI Sinfonia in B-flat Major \nItalian violinist and conductor Fabio Biondi\, world-renowned for “blazing\, fierce performances” (Washington Classical Review) with his ensemble Europa Galante\, leads a high-voltage program centered around Vivaldi\, those who inspired him (Geminiani and Corelli)\, and those he inspired\, like Nardini and Pugnani. Concertmaster Gina DiBello joins Biondi for Vivaldi’s Concerto for 2 Violins in G Minor. Make new discoveries and hear familiar favorites afresh! \nMusic of the Baroque Orchestra\nFabio Biondi\, conductor & violin\nGina DiBello\, violin
URL:https://northshorecenter.org/event/mob426/
LOCATION:George Van Dusen Theatre
CATEGORIES:Music of the Baroque
END:VEVENT
