UID:10001363-1776454200-1776454200@northshorecenter.org
SUMMARY:Bang Productions Presents: Jimmie Allen
DESCRIPTION:Jimmie Allen’s journey from Milton\, Delaware to Nashville is powered by equal parts grit and genre-bending ambition. After relocating to Music City in 2007\, Allen spent years sharpening his craft and building a sound that honors country’s storytelling tradition while leaning into today’s pop-forward energy. That persistence paid off with his 2018 debut album Mercury Lane—a personal nod to his hometown roots—and the breakout single “Best Shot\,” which became his first Billboard Country Airplay No. 1. A storyteller at heart\, Allen writes with the confidence of an artist who built his career the hard way. \nAllen quickly proved he wasn’t a one-hit newcomer. He followed with “Make Me Want To\,” earning a second Billboard Country Airplay chart-topper\, and later notched a third No. 1 with “Freedom Was a Highway\,” a stadium-ready collaboration with Brad Paisley. Along the way\, Allen established himself as one of the country’s most fearless collaborators. His Bettie James era spotlighted the duet “This Is Us” with Noah Cyrus and expanded into Bettie James Gold Edition with high-profile features including Nelly\, Tim McGraw\, and Mickey Guyton. \nIndustry recognition followed. Allen was named ACM New Male Artist and CMA New Artist of the Year in 2021 and earned a GRAMMY nomination for Best New Artist\, signaling crossover impact backed by real radio success. He’s also become a standout on camera\, co-hosting the Academy of Country Music Awards alongside Dolly Parton and Gabby Barrett and appearing as a featured artist on Apple TV+’s My Kind of Country. \nIn 2022\, Allen continued to stretch the format on Tulip Drive\, pairing heartfelt songwriting—highlighted by the tribute “Down Home”—with bold\, headline-grabbing collaborations including Jennifer Lopez and CeeLo Green. On stage and in the studio\, he blends big hooks with lived-in detail\, delivering songs that feel both radio-ready and personal. His music celebrates hometown pride\, love\, and resilience—connecting with fans across country\, pop\, and beyond.
URL:https://northshorecenter.org/event/jimmie-allen/
LOCATION:George Van Dusen Theatre
CATEGORIES:Music,North Shore Center Presents
END:VEVENT
